=================================================
fix the order of Parser expression tree when converted into IR
Example:

var x: number = 5 + 0.01 * 19^6 * 10 / 10

INTO

    push int64 5
    push string 0.01
    push int64 19
    push int64 6
    POW
    MUL  <----- so it multiplies with 0.01 first with the pow result, not 10
    push int64 10
    MUL
    push int64 10
    DIV
    ADD
    declare global [num64] 1: x

NOT

    push int64 5
    push string 0.01
    push int64 19
    push int64 6
    POW
    push int64 10
    push int64 10
    DIV
    MUL
    MUL
    ADD
    declare global [num64] 1: x

NOTE:
var z: number = 156211616/214 * 92140 - 2525 + 252525197 % 6723525 ^ 535266 -99
converts incorrectly, make sure it works

=================================================

ADD BRACKETS
Example:

var x: number = (5 + 0.01) * 19^6 * 10 / 10

INTO

    push int64 5
    push string 0.01
    ADD
    push int64 19
    push int64 6
    POW
    push int64 10
    push int64 10
    DIV
    MUL
    MUL
    declare global [num64] 1: x

NOT

    push int64 5
    push string 0.01
    push int64 19
    push int64 6
    POW
    push int64 10
    push int64 10
    DIV
    MUL
    MUL
    ADD <---- priority was never moved
    declare global [num64] 1: x

=================================================

SUPPORT ALL TYPES OF OPERATIONS
For now non mathematical operations (but including NEG and CALL)
make the program crash, please implement support for it

